# Eva & Adam — environment contract
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Every variable below is REQUIRED;
# lib/env.ts throws at boot if any is missing or malformed.
#
# Rule: no secret is ever prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_. Only the Supabase URL is public.
#
# THREE THINGS THAT WILL COST YOU AN HOUR EACH IF NOBODY TELLS YOU.
#
# 1. Escape every `$` in the two scrypt hashes as `\$`. Next.js expands
#    `$VAR` in .env files the way docker-compose does, so an unescaped
#    `scrypt$16384$8$1$...` is torn into variable references before
#    lib/env.ts ever sees it, and the error you get names the wrong thing.
#
#    Quoting is NOT the alternative. Single and double quotes do not
#    stop the expansion in this stack (measured on Next 16.2.12:
#    'scrypt$16384$...' arrives just as mangled as the raw form, in
#    both @next/env and the Turbopack dev server). `\$` is the only
#    form both parsers deliver intact. If someone tells you to
#    single-quote instead, they are re-arming this trap.
#
# 2. Never define these variables in BOTH the process environment and
#    this file. Each source works alone; the combination does not.
#    Measured on Next 16.2.12 (`next dev`, Turbopack): a correct
#    `\$`-escaped .env.local boots, correct process-env-only boots,
#    but process env + .env.local together fails lib/env.ts with
#    "malformed" — even though either source alone is valid. This is
#    exactly how the Playwright e2e suite dies at webServer boot when
#    a developer .env.local exists (its config injects fixture env on
#    top of your file), and the error will point you at your hashes,
#    which are fine. If a boot refuses with "malformed" hashes you
#    have checked twice: look for a second definition source, not a
#    typo.
#
# 3. NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL has to point at something that answers, even
#    locally. `POST /api/session` reads `auth_attempts` before it looks at
#    the password, and the rate limiter fails CLOSED — a network error
#    there is treated the same as being actively under attack, so a
#    placeholder hostname makes every login 503. Point at a real (even
#    empty) Supabase project, or at anything that returns `[]` to GET and
#    201 to POST under /rest/v1/*.

# Public — safe to ship to the browser
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# Server-only — never exposed to the client
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
APP_PASSWORD_HASH=
VAULT_PASSPHRASE_HASH=
SESSION_SECRET=

# Optional — the only variable in this file that is not required.
# Gates the margin (docs/04-features/AI-PARTNER-SPEC.md) and nothing else.
# Without it the margin's route answers 503 and the rest of the app is
# unaffected. Its offline evals run with no key at all.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
